<title>UK: LME copper stabilises, nickel tumbles at end AM.</title>
<headline>LME copper stabilises, nickel tumbles at end AM.</headline>
<text>
<p>COPPER - Holds above support at $2,250 despite downside test, ends $18 down at $2,260. Cash/threes backwardation eases further to $180/$190 due to sizeable stock rise. Cash/day trades up to $19 in second ring.</p>
<p>ALUMINIUM - Bounces off early low to just softer $1,560.</p>
<p>ZINC - Avoiding copper trauma, unchanged.</p>
<p>NICKEL - Falls $125 to $6,750 as funds liquidate, hit stops.</p>
<p>OTHERS - Lower.</p>
</text>
